<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udjahorresnet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udjahorresnet was an Egyptian official, physician and priest of Neith at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> who served the last Saite kings and then the Persian conquerors. His inscribed statue, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatican-museums">Vatican Museums</a>, records that he helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-ii">Cambyses II</a> compose his pharaonic titles after the conquest of 525 BCE and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> sent him to restore the medical school at Sais.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/udjahorresnet.jpg" alt="Udjahorresnet" width="320" height="542" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Neithsabes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museo_Gregoriano_004a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
